# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) for local dev. Never commit .env.local.
#
# Env var names are locked by the tech note (P1-F02-T03, docs/tech/). The
# client only ever reads tiles/glyphs/sprite URLs from these three: it never
# hardcodes a basemap host, so the real Bangkok tile host (Cloudflare
# R2/Pages, D-008) drops in later without a code change.
#
# --- Temporary fixture (TL-S08) ---
# There is no self-hosted Bangkok PMTiles extract yet (that is P1-F02-T06).
# Until then, point at a public Protomaps fixture so the spike page has
# something to render. This is a full-planet build meant for exactly this
# kind of evaluation: PMTiles uses HTTP range requests, so the browser only
# fetches the small byte ranges for the tiles actually on screen, not the
# whole archive. Swap this for the Bangkok extract's URL once P1-F02-T06
# publishes one (see apps/client/README.md).
VITE_TILES_URL=https://build.protomaps.com/20230925.pmtiles

# Protomaps' hosted basemap glyphs/sprite (Thai-capable font stack). The
# art-directed style (P1-F03-T12) may point these at self-hosted assets
# instead so the client does not depend on an external CDN in production.
VITE_GLYPHS_URL=https://protomaps.github.io/basemaps-assets/fonts/{fontstack}/{range}.pbf
VITE_SPRITE_URL=https://protomaps.github.io/basemaps-assets/sprites/v4/light
